# SQL's `like` with a prefix pattern: DS0105 suggesting `startswith`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where customerId like 'c-%'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..43
  PIPELINE@0..42
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..42
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..42
        NAME_REF@21..31
          IDENT@21..31 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
        IDENT@32..36 "like"
        WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
        LITERAL@37..42
          STRING@37..42 "'c-%'"
  WHITESPACE@42..43 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `like` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:33
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where customerId like 'c-%'
  |                                 ^^^^ this is SQL's pattern match
  |
  = help: use `startswith`: `customerId startswith 'c-'`
  = note: `startswith` ignores case; `startswith_cs` matches case exactly
